---
const GETS = [
  {
    k: 'Profiles',
    h: 'A profile that changes the output.',
    p: 'Vocabulary, style, delivery and model belong to whatever you are working on. A commit message and a mail to a client are not the same job.',
  },
  {
    k: 'Models',
    h: 'Four lanes, picked per job.',
    p: 'The local runtime as a real option, not a weekend of configuration. Picked per profile, not once for the whole app.',
  },
  {
    k: 'The record',
    h: 'It shows what it changed.',
    p: 'Raw and delivered are stored apart. Every rule that fired is named, and audio it could not hear is marked as a gap instead of guessed at.',
  },
  {
    k: 'Credentials',
    h: 'Your keys, your machine.',
    p: 'API keys live in the operating system secret store, and the config file is scrubbed on save. Nothing leaves for anywhere you did not pick.',
  },
  {
    k: 'Sources',
    h: 'Bring audio in.',
    p: 'An uploaded file, or a pasted video, podcast or direct audio link, becomes the same kind of record as something you said out loud.',
  },
  {
    k: 'Licence',
    h: 'AGPL-3.0, the whole thing.',
    p: 'No open core with the good half behind a login. Read it before you decide anything.',
  },
];
---
<section class="sec" id="what">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="sec__head rise">
      <h2>The dictation half, done properly.</h2>
    </div>

    <ul class="gets rise" data-d="1">
      {GETS.map((g) => (
        <li>
          <span class="k">{g.k}</span>
          <h3>{g.h}</h3>
          <p>{g.p}</p>
        </li>
      ))}
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>
